"A collective term for gfo-base:Stratum and gfo-base:Level."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"A collective term for gfo-base:Stratum and gfo-base:Level."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "A collective term for gfo-base:Stratum and gfo-base:Level."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"A function F is a universal (conceptual structure) defined in purely teleological terms with respect to a given goal G which commonly is ascribed by means of has-function relation to entities that are the realizations of the function F, execute such a realization or are intended to do it."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"A function F is a universal (conceptual structure) defined in purely teleological terms with respect to a given goal G which commonly is ascribed by means of has-function relation to entities that are the realizations of the function F, execute such a realization or are intended to do it."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "A function F is a universal (conceptual structure) defined in purely teleological terms with respect to a given goal G which commonly is ascribed by means of has-function relation to entities that are the realizations of the function F, execute such a realization or are intended to do it."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"A material structure is an individual which satisfies the following conditions: it is a presential, it occupies space, it is a bearer of qualities, but other entities cannot have it as quality, and it consists of an amount of substrate, and it instantiates a persistant (\"has identity\")."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"A material structure is an individual which satisfies the following conditions: it is a presential, it occupies space, it is a bearer of qualities, but other entities cannot have it as quality, and it consists of an amount of substrate, and it instantiates a persistant (\"has identity\")."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "A material structure is an individual which satisfies the following conditions: it is a presential, it occupies space, it is a bearer of qualities, but other entities cannot have it as quality, and it consists of an amount of substrate, and it instantiates a persistant (\"has identity\")."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"A presential exists wholly at exactly one time boundary."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"A presential exists wholly at exactly one time boundary."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "A presential exists wholly at exactly one time boundary."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"A process without an instantaneous change at any of its inner time boundaries is called a state."@en <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "A process without an instantaneous change at any of its inner time boundaries is called a state."@en .
"A situation is a special configuration which can be comprehended as a whole and satisfies certain conditions of unity, which are imposed by relations and categories associated with the situation. Herein, we consider situations to be the most complex kind of presentials."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"A situation is a special configuration which can be comprehended as a whole and satisfies certain conditions of unity, which are imposed by relations and categories associated with the situation. Herein, we consider situations to be the most complex kind of presentials."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "A situation is a special configuration which can be comprehended as a whole and satisfies certain conditions of unity, which are imposed by relations and categories associated with the situation. Herein, we consider situations to be the most complex kind of presentials."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"Abstract"@en <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "Abstract"@en .
"According to (Poli, 2001), the basic structure of the material stratum is a distinction of physical, chemical and biological levels. These levels can be further refined."@en <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "According to (Poli, 2001), the basic structure of the material stratum is a distinction of physical, chemical and biological levels. These levels can be further refined."@en .
"Action"@en <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "Action"@en .
"Actions are occurrents which are caused by some presential (the agent) at every (inner and outer) time-boundary of the chronoid framing the occurrent."@en <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "Actions are occurrents which are caused by some presential (the agent) at every (inner and outer) time-boundary of the chronoid framing the occurrent."@en .
"Amount of substrate"@en <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "Amount of substrate"@en .
"An item is everything which is not a set. Also called ur-element."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"An item is everything which is not a set. Also called ur-element."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "An item is everything which is not a set. Also called ur-element."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
