"Process"@en <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "Process"@en .
"Processes are a special kind of occurrent. Processes are directly in time, they have characteristics which cannot be captured by a collection of time boundaries."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"Processes are a special kind of occurrent. Processes are directly in time, they have characteristics which cannot be captured by a collection of time boundaries."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "Processes are a special kind of occurrent. Processes are directly in time, they have characteristics which cannot be captured by a collection of time boundaries."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"Processes where all non-coinciding internal boundaries are intrinsic changes. These turn out as purely continuous processes, described e.g. in physics by differential equations."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"Processes where all non-coinciding internal boundaries are intrinsic changes. These turn out as purely continuous processes, described e.g. in physics by differential equations."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "Processes where all non-coinciding internal boundaries are intrinsic changes. These turn out as purely continuous processes, described e.g. in physics by differential equations."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"Processual role"@en <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "Processual role"@en .
"Processual roles are dependent processes. They are roles with a process as context."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
"Processual roles are dependent processes. They are roles with a process as context."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> "Processual roles are dependent processes. They are roles with a process as context."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
