<https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Change> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Change> .
<https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Change> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A change in the technical sense refers to a pair of process boundaries. Either at coinciding boundaries (then it comes close to notions like ``punctual'' or ``instantaneous event'' as well as ``moment'' -- in a temporal reading), or at boundaries at the opposite ends of a process of arbitrary extension.\nThe notion of change is relative to contradictory conditions between which a transition takes place. These contradictions refer to some collection of pairwise disjoint universals."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
