<https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Persistant> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Persistants are GFO's way to capture identity over time.\nGFO pursues an approach which accounts for persistence by means of a suitable universal whose instances are presentials. Such universals are called persistants. These do not change and they can be used to explain how presentials which have different properties at different times can nevertheless be the same."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
