<https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Social_stratum> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass> <https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Social_stratum> .
<https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Social_stratum> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Social_stratum> .
<https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Social_stratum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "On the one hand, the social stratum is divided into Agents and Institutions. Agents are the bearers of the social roles that humans play. Institutions are defined as systems of interrelated social components. On the other hand, a social system can be seen as a network in which businesses, politics, art, language (and many other facets) both present their own features and influence each other."@en .
