<https://w3id.org/gfo/base/Spatial_boundary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Boundaries of regions are surfaces, boundaries of surfaces are lines, and boundaries of lines are points. As in the case of time-boundaries, spatial boundaries have no independent existence, i.e. they depend on the spatial entity of which they are boundaries."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
